{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0ae6d7ffd82b1d06","name":"DC0052 \"Intergalactic\" Speeder","source":{"id":"source:reference-0ae6d7ffd82b1d06","title":"DC0052 \"Intergalactic\" Speeder","revision":19869,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:45:58Z","sha256":"e41d01f4e0b2af445caf009a4b8dbcc14e3d3844ee62b68cb7ea7396d6f6b8a8","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19869","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=DC0052%20%22Intergalactic%22%20Speeder&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0ae6d7ffd82b1d06","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Among the different vehicles available to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," on Coruscant is the small Daystar Craft DC0052 \"Intergalactic\" Speeder. ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"}," maintains a small fleet of sixteen of these ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"}," to permit travel around the planet without having to rely on public transportation or checking out a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," for such a short trip. Daystar Craft's main selling points for the little speeder are its streamlined body and twin thrust pod system that propels the craft up to 800 kilometers per hour. Coupled with the Vehicle's range of 2,000 kilometers and ceiling height of 170 kilometers, the DC0052 allows its occupant to reach virtually anywhere he wants to go on the planet.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The speeder's resemblance to various ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," in production around the galaxy helped it earn the nickname \"Intergalactic,\" despite the fact that it cannot achieve suborbital altitudes. Although Daystar officials never adopt the nickname, the moniker sticks nonetheless.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A feature added specifically to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," variant of the speeder is what Daystar calls a \"Drop-Deployment\" panel, which allows the pilot to drop out of the speeder at a second's notice without bringing it to a halt. Once activated, the speeder is set to autopilot, while the hatch drops open and lets the occupant fallout of the DC0052.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["DC0052 \"Intergalactic\" Speeder Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 10), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 13; +1 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","ch